# One | EXT | Narrow Lane | NIGHT | troffea, husband | Not stop | The sixth night. Torches. A serving girl at a window is swaying. Then she is in the lane | Others join | 5 | crowd=50, dance
# Four Hundred | INT | Council Chamber | DAY | doctor_wendel, ammeister | Prescribe | Not the stars. Hot blood. The cure is more dancing: clear the halls, hire pipers, pay strong men to keep them up | The city hires a band | 5 | crowd=30
# Four Hundred | EXT | Horse Market, Stage | DAY | troffea, doctor_wendel, ammeister | Dance it out | A stage like a scaffold. Pipes, drums, four hundred dancers, porters gripping them under the arms. The crowd at the edge begins to nod in time | Music spreads it | 8 | crowd=500, dance, props=stage+pipes and drums
# Four Hundred | EXT | Horse Market, Stage | DUSK | troffea, doctor_wendel | Try to stop | A child at the rope is swaying. {troffea} fights her own legs to reach her, and cannot. A man beside her falls and is not moving | The first deaths | 6 | crowd=500, dance, stunts=collapse
# The Shrine | INT | Council Chamber | NIGHT | doctor_wendel, ammeister | Reverse it | The physician begs: no music. The councillor does the sum again. Ban the pipes; pull down the stage; send them to the saint | | 4 | crowd=30
# The Shrine | INT | Hill Grotto | DAY | troffea, doctor_wendel | Stop | Wagons, three days, red shoes, oil, three circuits of an altar. She sits. She takes the shoes off. She sleeps | The dancing stops | 6 | crowd=120, dance, props=red shoes
